  "assistant_text": "I’ve set up a comparison model, but it cannot yet tell us which hiring path leads under your circumstances.\n\nIt includes:\n- **Hire a Tech Lead**\n- **Hire Two Developers**\n- Also, for context: **Hire One Developer** and **Continue Current Staffing**\n\nThe key uncertainty is whether your present constraint is **technical leadership, prioritisation and coordination** or simply **engineering delivery capacity**. The model currently has six unknown starting factors, and “continue current staffing” has no stated effect, so it cannot be compared.\n\nI can use the following **machine-authored assumptions** as a first test — these are not measurements. Please adopt or correct them:\n\n**Starting position**\n- Tech-lead capacity: **4 capacity points (0–10)** — some leadership exists, but a bottleneck remains.\n- Developer capacity: **8 capacity points (0–20)** — a modest existing delivery base.\n- Work prioritisation: **60 index points (0–100)** — workable, with meaningful room to improve.\n- Engineering coordination: **60 index points (0–100)** — adequate, but not yet strong at scale.\n- Delivery capacity: **12 capacity points (0–30)** — below the middle of the model range.\n- New-hire ramp-up: **50 index points (0–100)** — a typical moderate ramp-up burden.\n\n**What each hire would set**\n- Hire a Tech Lead → Tech-lead capacity: **8**\n- Hire One Developer → Developer capacity: **10**\n- Hire Two Developers → Developer capacity: **12**\n\nThese assumptions deliberately separate the direct capacity added by developers from the leadership/coordination effect of a Tech Lead. They do not yet represent salary, time-to-hire, or your exact team size.\n\nIf you approve this starting point, I’ll save it and run the comparison.\n\nThe model was saved. Questions this model does not answer yet: What is the current team size and existing technical-leadership capacity? How will productivity be measured (for example, throughput, cycle time, quality-adjusted output, or business outcomes)? What hiring timeline and ramp-up period should be evaluated? Are budget, salary, or headcount constraints material to this decision? Is the current primary constraint insufficient engineering capacity, weak technical direction/prioritisation, or both?",
